        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "This should now be resolved on latest `main`.\r\n\r\nIt indeed was an issue with filetype detection. It is done *after* buffer name is set which always ends with a Git command used. So in case of `:Git show HEAD file.lua` it had name ending with 'show HEAD file.lua' which `vim.filetype.match()` deduced to be a Lua file. This is a useful behavior in case of command like `:Git show HEAD:file.lua` but indeed is counter-intuitive for `:Git show HEAD file.lua`.\r\n\r\nAt the same time, the plain `:Git show HEAD` did not match based on buffer name and reached the stage of matching by buffer content to correctly produce \"git\" filetype. So the rather appropriate solution here seems to force first trying to detect \"git\" filetype based on the buffer content and only then fall back to `vim.filetype.match()`.",
            "created_at": "2024-07-26T15:13:09Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/1084#issuecomment-2252973938",
